  "title": "Fire in Shangfang Valley, and Then Rain",
  "year": "234",
  "summary": [
    "Zhuge Liang builds a supply depot in a gourd-shaped valley, garrisons it visibly with the wooden transports, and lets Sima Yi discover it. Sima Yi comes in with his two sons; the mouth is sealed, the mines are fired, and the whole valley burns.",
    "Then a thunderstorm breaks directly overhead and puts it out, and they ride out through the ash. Zhuge Liang, watching from the ridge: 'Man may plan, but heaven decides.'"
  ],
  "history": "Invented. It exists so that the book can say out loud what it has been circling for twenty chapters: that Zhuge Liang is not losing to Sima Yi.",
